{#
  T-4.13 — the quick product view.

  IT IS T-2.10's SHEET, NOT A SECOND OVERLAY. Every one of this task's focus
  criteria — focus in, focus trapped, focus back to the trigger, `Esc`, backdrop,
  scroll lock, centred dialog above tablet — is already the primitive's, and the
  primitive gets them from `<dialog>` + `showModal()` rather than from code that
  would have to be written again here. This file supplies a body and nothing else.

  THE TITLE IS HIDDEN, NOT ABSENT. The artboard draws no heading in the sheet's
  header — the product's brand and name sit in the body, under the close button.
  An unnamed dialog is announced as just "dialog", so the name is kept and only
  the pixels are dropped, which is exactly what `title_hidden` exists for. The
  placeholder below is replaced with the real product name the moment it arrives,
  so the dialog is never announced with the wrong name — only with a generic one
  while it is still loading, which is true at that moment.

  ONE SHEET FOR THE WHOLE PAGE, not one per card. A grid of thirty products would
  otherwise put thirty dialogs in the document, twenty-nine of them describing
  products nobody asked about — and the fetch-on-open criterion exists precisely
  to stop that. `master.twig` includes this once; `quick-view.js` fills it.

  THE BODY IS EMPTY ON PURPOSE and starts as a skeleton. Nothing about a product
  is known until a card is clicked, so anything rendered here at page load would
  be either wrong or a second copy of data the card already holds.
#}
{% set quick_view_body %}
    <div class="quick-view" data-quick-view-root>
        {#
          The skeleton stands in a box the layout has already reserved — the
          `min-block-size` on `.quick-view` — so the real content does not push
          the sheet taller when it lands. A placeholder that sizes itself is a
          layout shift waiting for a slow connection.
        #}
        <div class="quick-view__loading" data-quick-view-loading>
            {% include 'components.ui.skeleton' with {
                lines: 3,
                label: trans('theme.product.quick_view_loading')
            } only %}
        </div>

        {#
          `hidden` rather than empty: the container is in the DOM from the start
          so the script has somewhere to write, and out of the accessibility tree
          until it holds something.
        #}
        <div class="quick-view__content" data-quick-view-content hidden></div>

        <p class="quick-view__error" data-quick-view-error hidden role="alert"></p>
    </div>
{% endset %}

{% include 'components.ui.bottom-sheet' with {
    id:           'quick-view-sheet',
    title:        trans('theme.product.quick_view'),
    title_hidden: true,
    body:         quick_view_body
} %}
